,"orientation":"h","x":0,"y":1.08,"yanchor":"bottom"}},                        {"responsive": true, "displaylogo": false}                    )                };            </script>        </div><p>Hatched timing bars denote combinations with at least one failed certificate. They remain visible to distinguish fast inaccurate answers from slow successful solves; they do not contribute as successes to the profiles.</p><h2>G1 humanoid QPs</h2><p>These are three fixed application QPs, with 18,549 to 193,566 variables. G1 calls use up to eight TBB/solver threads on CPUs 0–7, one numerical-library thread, a 300-second watchdog and a 16 GiB memory cap. External solvers retain their recorded supported thread settings; OSQP uses its serial sparse backend. Objective factors, original inverse sigmas and application damping are preserved. No additional objective regularization is added. All original feasibility, stationarity, sign and absolute-gap thresholds are 1e-7; complementarity is recorded separately.</p><p>The table uses primary complete-call times, not medians. GTSAM times exclude native factor reconstruction; external setup/solve times exclude separately recorded Hessian conversion. Five additional G1SP20 observations are available in the JSON for the retained successful external and Sparse Dual calls; other G1 results are single observations. Watchdog entries are censored lower bounds, never completed solves. DAQP was not run on G1.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Capture</th><th>Solver</th><th>Primary seconds</th><th>Original certificate / outcome</th><th>Absolute gap</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>G1SP20</td><td>DAQP</td><td>—</td><td>not run</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>G1SP20</td><td>GTSAM Dense Dual</td><td>—</td><td>memory_limit</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>G1SP20</td><td>GTSAM Sparse Dual</td><td>3.697</td><td>certified</td><td>1.68e-13</td></tr><tr><td>G1SP20</td><td>ProxQP</td><td>1.002</td><td>certified</td><td>1.57e-08</td></tr><tr><td>G1SP20</td><