+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "gradients-guide-noise",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Learning a temperature-dependent noise model\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The previous example put the learnable quantity in the residual $e=x-z$.\n",
+    "Measurement $\\sigma$ lives in the noise model instead. Pass the `Diagonal` or\n",
+    "`Isotropic` model itself to `noiseGradient`; it returns $\\partial L/\\partial\\sigma$\n",
+    "summed over every active factor holding that exact instance, and no residual\n",
+    "`parameterVjp` is required. Stock factors such as `PriorFactorDouble` work as-is.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Models are matched by identity, not by value, so pass the same object you gave\n",
+    "the factors. The result has one entry per sigma for a `Diagonal` and one shared\n",
+    "entry for an `Isotropic`. Construct learned models with `smart=False`:\n",
+    "otherwise equal sigmas collapse a `Diagonal` into an `Isotropic`, and a sigma\n",
+    "of exactly 1 collapses into a parameter-free `Unit` model.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "A thermometer's reading of a constant $x^\\star_{\\mathrm{true}}=0$ gets worse as\n",
+    "the device heats up: $\\sigma(T)=\\sigma_0+\\alpha T$ with known $\\sigma_0=0.1$\n",
+    "and true $\\alpha^\\star=1$. Two unary factors constrain one scalar $x$:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "- cold, $T=0$, $z=0$, $\\sigma=0.1$, fixed;\n",
+    "- hot, $T=1$, $z=2$ (a bad reading), $\\sigma=\\sigma_0+\\alpha T$, learned.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The loss is $\\tfrac12(x^\\star)^2$. Starting at $\\alpha=0$ makes the hot factor\n",
+    "over-trusted, so $x^\\star$ sits near the outlier. Gradient steps on $\\alpha$\n",
+    "alone raise $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{hot}}$ and pull $x^\\star$ back toward $0$.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "A network that predicts $\\sigma$ should end with a map that keeps the output\n",
+    "positive (for example `softplus` or `exp`), and typically a small floor so\n",
+    "$\\sigma$ never reaches $0$."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "id": "gradients-guide-noise-code",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "key_x = X(1)\n",
+    "sigma0 = 0.1\n",
+    "alpha_true = 1.0\n",
+    "alpha = 0.0\n",
+    "T_hot = 1.0\n",
+    "lr = 0.1\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "def sigma_hot(a):\n",
+    "    return sigma0 + a * T_hot\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "def solve_temperature(a):\n",
+    "    temp_graph = gtsam.NonlinearFactorGraph()\n",
+    "    temp_graph.add(gtsam.PriorFactorDouble(\n",
+    "        key_x, 0.0, gtsam.noiseModel.Isotropic.Sigma(1, sigma0),\n",
+    "    ))\n",
+    "    hot = gtsam.noiseModel.Isotropic.Sigma(1, sigma_hot(a), False)  # smart=False\n",
+    "    temp_graph.add(gtsam.PriorFactorDouble(key_x, 2.0, hot))\n",
+    "    temp_initial = gtsam.Values()\n",
+    "    temp_initial.insert(key_x, 0.0)\n",
+    "    return temp_graph, hot, gtsam.GaussNewtonOptimizer(temp_graph, temp_initial).optimize()\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "_, _, x0 = solve_temperature(alpha)\n",
+    "print(f\"init   x*={x0.atDouble(key_x):.4f}  σ_hot={sigma_hot(alpha):.3f}\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "for _ in range(20):\n",
+    "    temp_graph, hot, temp_values = solve_temperature(alpha)\n",
+    "    cotangents = gtsam.VectorValues()\n",
+    "    cotangents.insert(key_x, np.array([temp_values.atDouble(key_x)]))  # dL/dx for L=1/2 (x*)^2, 0 is true state\n",
+    "    dL_dsigma = gtsam.Gradients(temp_graph, temp_values).noiseGradient(cotangents, hot)\n",
+    "    alpha -= lr * dL_dsigma[0] * T_hot\n",
+    "    alpha = max(alpha, 0.0)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "_, _, x1 = solve_temperature(alpha)\n",
+    "print(f\"step20 x*={x1.atDouble(key_x):.4f}  σ_hot={sigma_hot(alpha):.3f}  α={alpha:.3f}  (α*={alpha_true})\")\n",
+    "assert x1.atDouble(key_x) < x0.atDouble(key_x)\n",
+    "assert sigma_hot(alpha) > sigma0"
+   ]
+  },
