+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "c8c0416a",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "A **factor residual direction** specifies how the whitened factor residuals\n",
+    "change for a chosen parameter direction, holding the solved state fixed.\n",
+    "Increasing $z_0$ at unit rate gives the first factor direction $-1/\\sigma_0$\n",
+    "and leaves the second factor unchanged. `pushforward` returns the corresponding\n",
+    "change in the optimized state. Pairing the factor residual direction with the\n",
+    "`pullback` result gives the same loss derivative as `parameterGradient`."
